		(uuid "ec7b309c-cb03-486e-bbe5-ca6bf2fb5dbb")
	)
	(text "Backlight (Rev D): anodes on +5V,\nQ1 low-side. R4-R7 430R =\n~6.9 mA/LED @ Vf 2.0 V (assumed,\nLED P/N unknown); ~4.5 mA @ 3.0 V.\nQ1 Ic <= 30 mA, Ib ~2.4 mA (R14).\nR8 10K holds GPIO15 low at boot."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 235.712 80.518 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "edae0767-049b-4f9f-82b8-305ae3b38313")
	)
	(text_box "\nEnabling the chip:\nIf you're using a bare-bone ESP-## board by AI Thinker,\nyou have to add some resistors to turn on the ESP8266, \nand to select the right boot mode.\n\n1.) Enable the chip by connecting the CH_PD (Chip Power\n	Down, sometimes labeled CH_EN or chip enable) pin to\n	VCC through a 10KΩ resistor.\n2.) Disable SD-card boot by connecting GPIO15 to ground\n	through a 10KΩ resistor.\n3.) Select normal boot mode by connecting GPIO0 to VCC\n	through a 10KΩ resistor.\n4.) Prevent random resets by connecting the RST (reset) \n	pin to VCC through a 10KΩ resistor.\n5.) Make sure you don't have anything connected to GPIO2."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 15.24 156.2099 0)
		(size 74.93 44.4573)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 1.524)
			(type solid)
			(color 0 0 194 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "94df8ba9-5306-4d71-a589-9d6853459e06")
	)
